# The Cocoa display server's accepted differences from the X11 reference
# (tests/cocoa.sh). ref.sh turns gcon's antialias attribute off, so this
# is Core Graphics's aliased drawing, whose rule for which edge pixels a
# shape covers is not quite X's (about 10% more pixels than differed when
# recorded); text is CoreText's. Drawops, patterns, fills, copies and
# images must match exactly. Format as tests/ref/tolerance.
#
# name      pixels  output
clipcopy    780     same     # edges of slanted lines, a circle
lines       510     same     # edges of slanted lines, arcs
shapes      440     same     # edges of circles, arcs, polygons
text        -1      differs  # CoreText's fonts
